      <h2>Article 3: Warning &mdash; medical device, intended purpose and limits</h2>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <p><strong>PARKIWATCH is a Class IIa Software as a Medical Device (SaMD) intended for the continuous, passive detection and quantitative assessment of kinematic patterns representative of tremor, bradykinesia and dyskinesia in adults with Parkinson&rsquo;s Disease. It is not intended to diagnose Parkinson&rsquo;s Disease, or to recommend or modify specific pharmacological therapy independently. Its outputs are adjunctive to, and must be interpreted within the context of, standard clinical assessment and the treating healthcare professional&rsquo;s judgment.</strong></p>
        <p>PARKIWATCH is used under the supervision of your treating healthcare professional. It is intended for adults with Parkinson&rsquo;s Disease who are being treated and followed by a licensed healthcare professional.</p>
        <p>The Koios Care Service is not an emergency response system and should not be used as a substitute for professional medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always seek the advice of your physician or other qualified health provider with any questions you may have regarding a medical condition. Never disregard professional medical advice or delay in seeking it because of something you have read or interpreted from the Koios Care Service.</p>
      </div>
      <p>Please read the Instructions for Use carefully before using the Koios Care Service: <a href="/ifu-patients">Instructions for Use for patients</a> &middot; <a href="/ifu-hcps">Instructions for Use for healthcare professionals</a>.</p>

      <h2>Article 4: Service description &mdash; intended use</h2>
      <p>The Koios Care Service is designed to give Users and their treating healthcare professionals objective information on kinematic patterns between clinic visits. This includes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Passive collection of motion data from a compatible third-party smartwatch or wrist-worn sensor</li>
        <li>Validated kinematic measures representative of tremor, bradykinesia and dyskinesia</li>
        <li>Supportive digital health measures, calculated alongside the validated kinematic measures</li>
        <li>Reports made available to healthcare professionals via a web-based dashboard and PDF reports</li>
      </ul>
      <p>The information provided by the Koios Care Service does not constitute medical advice and does not replace the judgment of your healthcare professional.</p>

      <h2>Article 5: Biometric Data collection and use</h2>
      <h3>(a) Purpose of collection and use</h3>
      <p>We collect and process your Biometric Data solely for the following purposes:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>To provide the core functionalities of the Koios Care Service, such as producing the validated kinematic measures and the supportive digital health measures described in the Instructions for Use</li>
        <li>To personalise your user experience within the Koios Care Service</li>
        <li>For internal analysis to improve the Koios Care Service&rsquo;s functionality, features, and user experience, provided such data is anonymised or pseudonymised where feasible</li>
        <li>To support Parkinson&rsquo;s disease symptom tracking and quality of life assessment</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We will not collect, use, or store your Biometric Data for any purposes other than those disclosed in these Terms and our Privacy Policy without your explicit consent.</p>
      <h3>(b) Explicit consent</h3>
      <p><strong>Your use of the Koios Care Service and its features that collect Biometric Data constitutes your explicit consent to the collection, processing, use, and storage of your Biometric Data as described in these Terms and our Privacy Policy.</strong></p>
      <p>You will be asked to provide explicit consent before any Biometric Data is initially collected. You can withdraw your consent at any time by contacting us at info@koios.care. Withdrawing consent may limit or disable certain features of the Koios Care Service.</p>
      <h3>(c) Storage and security</h3>
      <p>We are committed to protecting your Biometric Data. We implement commercially reasonable technical, administrative, and physical security measures designed to protect your Biometric Data from unauthorised access, use, disclosure, alteration, or destruction. Details regarding our security practices are further outlined in our Privacy Policy.</p>
      <h3>(d) Data retention and deletion</h3>
      <p>We will retain your Biometric Data only for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected, as required to provide you with the Service, or as required by applicable law. Upon your request, account termination, or when the data is no longer needed for its initial purpose, we will permanently destroy or anonymise your Biometric Data in accordance with our Privacy Policy and applicable legal requirements.</p>

